gments: Pressure Control and Spoolable Technologies. The Pressure Control segment designs, manufactures, sells, and rents a range of wellheads and pressure control equipment under the Cactus Wellhead brand through its service centers. Its products are sold and rented primarily for onshore unconventional oil and gas wells for drilling, completion, and production phases. This segment also offers field services for its products and rental items to assist with the installation, maintenance, and handling of the equipment. The Spoolable Technologies segment designs, manufactures, and sells spoolable pipes and associated end fittings under the FlexSteel brand. Its products are primarily used in production, gathering, and takeaway pipelines to transport oil, gas, and other liquids. This segment also provides field services and rental items to assist with installation through service centers and pipe yards, as well as equipment and services. The company also offers repair and refurbishment services for pressure control equipment. Cactus, Inc. was founded in 2011 and is headquartered in Houston, Texas.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Scott J. Bender | CEO & Chairman of the Board | Age 71 | Compensation: $702,825 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $719K ranks in the below the sector median among Energy peers, with revenue growing 10%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $16K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["Cactus, Inc. Class A Common Sto is a mid-cap energy business with a $5.0B market cap on $1.1B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +16% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 45% against a 10% cost of capital \u2014 a 35-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.9%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 2.1\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 132% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":1.320425655476743},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $40.4M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"The commodity cycle \u2014 revenue and free cash flow are ultimately hostage to a price the company does not set, and the long-run energy-transition arc adds a structural overhang.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"ESG-driven capital flight and stranded asset risk \u2014 tightening climate policy and investor mandates raise the cost of capital and risk leaving reserves permanently in the ground.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Geopolitical supply shocks \u2014 wars, sanctions, and OPEC decisions create volatility that no hedging programme can fully neutralise.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Energy peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood","Growing faster than most Energy peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Among the least levered in Energy \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set","Energy sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter","Energy ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Cactus (WHD) Upgraded to Buy: Here's What You Should Know","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3027535/cactus-whd-upgraded-to-buy-here-s-what-you-should-know?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cyseop_template_12_zacks_rank_upgrade-3027535","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794339807.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["m_and_a","analyst_action"]},{"title":"Cactus (WHD) Could Be 15% Undervalued After Middle East Expansion And Strong Earnings","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/energy/nyse-whd/cactus/news/cactus-whd-could-be-15-undervalued-after-middle-east-expansi","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794277265.554,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.876,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"COP vs. WHD: Which Stock Is the Better Value Option?","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3026591/cop-vs-whd-which-stock-is-the-better-value-option?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cyseop_template_3-3026591","date":"2026-11-09","timestamp":1794238803.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.649,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Trading the Move, Not the Narrative: (WHD) Edition","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/34/Trading_the_Move,_Not_the_Narrative:_WHD_Edition_110426090402_1793801042.html","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793801042.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Is Cactus (WHD) Priced Too Richly For Its Earnings Story?",